<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Nan Ya July sales edge higher.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Nan Ya July sales edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nan Ya Plastics Corp, Taiwan's largest industrial enterprise, said on Tuesday its July sales edged 9.7 percent higher to T$8.022 billion from T$7.312 billion in July 1996.</p>
<p>The firm's combined January-July sales rose 6.9 percent to T$53.787 billion from T$50.299 billion registered in the same period in 1996, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not give profit figures.</p>
<p>Nan Ya has a sales target of T$94.921 billion for 1997.</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
